| API Gateway and Authentication | Routing, sessions, authorization, rate limits |
| Book Catalog | Book metadata, covers, search |
| Feed Service | Feed assembly and ranking |
| Posts and Ratings | Reader posts, reviews, expectation ratings |
| Social Graph | Follows, clubs, cohorts |
| Taste Matching | Similar-reader identification |
| Shelf Service | Reading status and personal collections |
| Notifications | Push and email notifications |
| Writing and Publishing | Drafts, chapters, published works |
| Feedback and Evaluation | Reader feedback, institutional evaluations |
| Institution Programs | Cohorts, showcases, competitions |
| Publisher Portal | Catalogs, promotions, analytics |
| Event Stream | Activity events and downstream processing |

The Phase 1 implementation should prioritize the components required for reader discovery, engagement, and trust.

# 13. Trust, Moderation and Content Integrity

Trust is central to Perch's value proposition.

The platform must prevent its reader-driven discovery model from becoming another promotion-driven feed.

Proposed requirements:

- Clearly distinguish organic posts from sponsored content.
- Prevent publishers from presenting sponsored posts as independent reviews.
- Provide mechanisms to report inappropriate or misleading content.
- Support moderation of reviews and user-generated content.
- Prevent duplicate or coordinated review manipulation where feasible.
- Make aggregated ratings transparent about the number of contributing readers.
- Avoid treating every rating as equally representative when displaying taste-based recommendations.

The platform should not assume that a negative review is automatically misleading or that a positive review is automatically trustworthy.

