# 15. Risks and Mitigation

| Risk | Potential Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Insufficient initial users | Empty or repetitive feed | Start with a focused reader community and seed relevant book content. |
| Low review contribution | Limited discovery data | Make posting simple and provide structured prompts. |
| Fake or manipulated reviews | Loss of credibility | Introduce reporting, moderation, and contribution transparency. |
| Cold-start recommendations | Irrelevant reader suggestions | Use onboarding preferences and genre-based discovery initially. |
| Commercial influence | Erosion of trust | Maintain clear sponsored labels and organic-content separation. |
| Scope expansion | Delayed MVP | Keep writer and publisher functionality outside Phase 1. |
| Catalog duplication | Poor book discovery | Use canonical book identifiers and catalog deduplication. |

# 16. MVP Acceptance Criteria

The first release should be considered functionally ready when:

- A reader can register and access Perch.
- A reader can discover books through a feed.
- A reader can search for and view book details.
- A reader can publish a book-related post.
- A reader submitting a review can provide an expectation-match rating.
- A reader can follow another reader.
- A reader can view relevant posts from followed readers.
- A reader can organize books into reading shelves.
- A reader can access external purchasing links.
- A reader can view other readers' opinions on a book.
- Core privacy, authorization, and content management requirements work as expected.

The first release does not need advanced AI recommendations, publisher dashboards, or a complete reading-club ecosystem.

# 17. Open Product Decisions

The following questions require validation before implementation.

| ID | Question | Why It Matters |
|---|---|---|
| OD-01 | Will Perch support only public profiles initially, or private profiles too? | Changes social graph and visibility rules. |
| OD-02 | Should users rate enjoyment separately from expectation match? | Establishes a more complete review model. |
| OD-03 | Should every post require a book association? | Determines whether general reading-related posts are supported. |
| OD-04 | Should feed ranking prioritize followed readers, similar readers, or a combination? | Defines the core discovery experience. |
| OD-05 | How will readers establish that they have actually read a book? | Affects review credibility. |
| OD-06 | Will reading clubs be included in the first MVP? | Affects development scope. |
| OD-07 | Which book metadata provider will be used? | Determines catalog integration. |
| OD-08 | How will expectation-match ratings be aggregated and displayed? | Directly affects trust and interpretation. |
| OD-09 | Will Perch initially target a particular language or geography? | Influences catalog, onboarding, and community strategy. |
| OD-10 | What is the minimum evidence required before opening Phase 2? | Prevents premature expansion. |

